//=====================================================
// Fetch ALL Execution Logs of this Execution Entry
//=====================================================
//
// Run Execute.bat after Tosca executions. Every log of every execution entry
// is read (newest first). import_results.py then stores only the logs that
// are not in the database yet and splits them into one report per execution
// (a gap of more than RUN_GAP_MINUTES, default 60, starts a new report). So:
//   - logs already imported earlier          -> skipped
//   - one execution since the last import    -> one new report
//   - several executions since the last one  -> one new report each
//
//=====================================================

For "->SORT(=>SUPERPART:ExecutionList->ExecutionLogs[Name==\"ActualLog\"]->TestCaseLogs,\"-StartTime\")" CallOnEach "scripts\\GetTestCaseLog.tcs"

Exit
